ull,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Fedora Linux 41 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV GFX1201) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIndirect lighting from a spotlight is influenced by the voxel size. Setting a higher subdivision level results in a decrease of indirect lighting radius.\n\n↓ From left to right, the subdivision levels are set to 64, 128 and 256 ↓\n\n(If the subdivision level is set to 512, then the indirect light spot simply disappears, which makes me quite certain that this is a bug)\n\n(VoxelGI off)![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f772d5c-4ce2-4808-8fbd-84eb14badb97)\n\n(VoxelGI on)![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/186297d2-9727-41bc-b502-08f9a93fc260)\n\n(VoxelGI Lighting)![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b532591c-8455-4144-9f22-dc489bb039e1)\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCopy a simple lighting test scene twice, and give each a VoxelGI node with different subdivision levels.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[voxelgi-spotlight-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20594728/voxelgi-spotlight-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mg